The function is already about as lean as it gets: one pointer check, one bounds check and one load. The rewrite keeps exactly the same logic and the same result for every input. It only adds `__builtin_expect` hints that tell the compiler the valid-profile path is the common case, so that path is laid out as straight-line code. Any speedup from this will be small.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetNum(void) const
{
    const auto* const p = profile;
    if (__builtin_expect(p != NULL, 1))
    {
        const auto idx = profileIndex;
        if (__builtin_expect(idx < p->numFields, 1))
            return p->fields[idx].num;
    }
    return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
}
```